#!/usr/bin/python3
"""loginnode-notify - ask users to move login-node work into Slurm allocations.

  loginnode-notify check                  config, transport and template sanity check
  loginnode-notify detect [--all-nodes]   scan the login nodes, start a new run (read-only)
  loginnode-notify review [--all | --pick 1,3,5-7 | -i] [filters]
                                          one row per user; choose who to contact
  loginnode-notify review --stale ...     same, for cleanup notices about orphaned
                                          servers (VS Code/Cursor/Jupyter > 30 days)
  loginnode-notify compose [--force]      one editable draft per selected user
  loginnode-notify add CATEGORY NETID... [--note TEXT] [--remove]
                                          flag users by hand (e.g. io_heavy); then review
  loginnode-notify names                  netID -> greeting for the run's selection
  loginnode-notify name NETID...          resolve names now (finger / getent)
  loginnode-notify selftest [--send]      one test message to yourself
  loginnode-notify send [--only U,V] [--self-test] [--send]
                                          deliver the drafts; dry run unless --send
  loginnode-notify report                 what the run selected and sent
  loginnode-notify log [N]                last N notify.log entries
  loginnode-notify recheck [--all-nodes]  contacted users who are still at it

`detect` starts a run in state/runs/<id>/ and records it in state/current; the
other commands use that run unless given --run ID. `send` re-checks every
recipient against notify.log just before delivering, so re-running it never
mails anyone twice in a run or within the cooldown.
"""

